From 5f2dcc3b375358b54e02f71b3f35b61844b06826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MRizky099 <mrizky793@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:02:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] docking: opt-in Fill tab widths and scrolling tab strips
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DockStyle gains `tab_sizing` (Natural | Fill) and `tab_overflow`
(Menu | Scroll). Fill stretches a group's tabs to share the strip evenly,
keeping wider labels at their natural width. Scroll keeps label widths and
scrolls the strip with the wheel or ‹ › arrows; the active tab scrolls into
view when it changes and a dragged tab near an end auto-scrolls. Tabs
scrolled out of view get no hit area; a drop past the last visible tab
inserts before the first hidden one. Pure helpers `tabs::fill` and
`tabs::scroll` sit next to `tabs::fit`, with unit tests. Defaults stay
Natural and Menu, so existing apps are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
